  "x-contract": {
    "task_id": "P02-T09",
    "visibility": "Internal explicit construction only. ModelCallIdentity and budget context are json:- Go values, never a client request body or deserialized authorization context.",
    "execution": "PrepareModelCall is readonly. A successful preparation is not a reservation, dispatch permit or payment receipt. The live budget source and certified upper-bound quoter are not installed in production during P02. Missing adapters fail closed, metadata_only cannot execute, and runtime_ready stays false.",
    "pricing": "The gateway input-only preconsume estimate is not a certified strict total-cost bound. Unknown pricing, unbounded pricing or malformed/mismatched/expired price certificates must reject before a runner can be called. Existing billing expressions and formulas are unchanged.",
    "limits": "Current text Agents allow one model call, no tools, at most 64 steps and 300000 accumulated execution ms; output tokens also use the existing relay validator. Policy intersection and caller lowering never enlarge a ceiling. Check positive remaining funding, Token quota, Run cost, counts, time/deadline and lease separately. Unlimited Token quota never removes concrete funding and Run limits.",
    "quota": "Wire observations use canonical nonnegative signed-int64 strings. Current calculation and per-call upper-bound preparation use the common.MaxQuota int32 boundary. No arithmetic or charging occurs in a DTO. Actual cost is NULL unless the minimal settled projection confirms both funding and Token outcomes; known free settlement may be 0.",
    "partial_facts": "prepared/dispatched/responded/rejected/outcome_unknown keep actual_quota NULL in this minimal projection. funding_state, token_state and preconsume_quota may preserve partial observed facts. The future P03 ledger must retain those observations even though this projection does not expose partial facts as a final usage item.",
    "identity": "IDs are canonical positive signed-int64 decimal strings in offline/wire projections. Go context uses positive int64 IDs, positive int32 attempt and safe positive lease values. caller_token_id is NULL for session calls; if present it must equal funding_token_id. This cross-field condition is enforced in Go, not standard JSON Schema.",
    "correlation": "Model usage validation requires a structurally valid settled gateway projection and exact Team/workspace/run/step/Agent/version/execution-user/funding/call/attempt/request/model/pricing identity. Charge quota equals the confirmed final call amount. Refunds require a different related_item_id and a quota no greater than the confirmed call actual charge. These are consistency checks only; trusted producer authentication, real reference lookup, source_event_key uniqueness and cross-row nonnegative net sums remain P03 responsibilities.",
    "logs": "consume_log_id is nullable and must be the raw persisted ID obtained from a trusted consume event in its configured log store. UI log IDs can be rewritten to display ordinals; request_id is a nonunique index and logs can be absent/duplicated/ClickHouse-backed. Neither an ID nor a matching log proves payment or allows retrying Settle. Confirmed settlement may have no log ID.",
    "persistence": "ag_gateway_calls, ag_usage_items and ag_budget_reservations remain P03 tables. This task introduces no migrations, database writes, quota reservations, model dispatch, settlement, refund or payment repair.",
    "schema_limits": "JSON Schema does not authenticate facts, verify database scope, correlate two objects, measure UTF-8 bytes, compare timestamps or enforce arithmetic. Go checks and actual local stub tests verify those semantic boundaries. No external schema references are used."
  }
}
